#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:9
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"Define the structure and quality bar for spec documents produced during "
"`/design` and `/diagnose` workflows. Specs are the handoff artifact "
"between the design phase and the delivery phase — they must be clear "
"enough for an engineer agent to follow without getting stuck, and "
"readable enough for a human to review before and learn from after "
"execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:13
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:15
msgid ""
"Load this skill when producing a spec document for any feature, "
"enhancement, or bug fix. The delivery lead should load this before "
"writing a spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:17
msgid "General conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:19
msgid "One spec per work item, saved as `spec.md`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:20
msgid "Write in plain markdown, no special syntax or RFC keywords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:21
msgid "Be concrete — name files, directories, components, functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:22
msgid "The Changes section is the most important section; it must be actionable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:23
msgid "Keep each section focused; do not repeat information across sections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:24
msgid "If information is unknown or requires investigation, say so explicitly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:25
msgid "Link to relevant issues, PRs, or external references when available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:27
msgid "File location"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:29
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Feature specs: `{hero_folder}/planning/features/{slug}/spec.md` Bug "
"specs: `{hero_folder}/planning/bugs/{slug}/spec.md`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:32
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The `{hero_folder}` defaults to `.hero` and is configurable via "
"`hero.json`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:34
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The `{slug}` is a short, lowercase, hyphenated identifier derived from "
"the work item title (e.g., `add-csv-export`, `login-timeout-race`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:36
msgid "Feature spec template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:38
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"# {title}\n"
"\n"
"## Context\n"
"Why this work exists. What prompted it. Links to issues or tickets.\n"
"Relevant history or prior decisions that affect this work.\n"
"\n"
"## Goal\n"
"What \"done\" looks like. One paragraph, concrete and testable.\n"
"This is the acceptance criteria in plain language.\n"
"\n"
"## Approach\n"
"Architecture and design decisions. How the feature fits into the existing"
" system.\n"
"Key technical choices already made and why.\n"
"Patterns to follow or avoid.\n"
"\n"
"## Changes\n"
"Ordered list of concrete changes to make. Each item should name specific "
"files\n"
"or components and describe what to do clearly enough that an engineer can"
" execute\n"
"without additional context.\n"
"\n"
"1. {description of first change}\n"
"   - {specific detail}\n"
"   - {specific detail}\n"
"2. {description of second change}\n"
"   - {specific detail}\n"
"3. ...\n"
"\n"
"## Mockups\n"
"Optional. Visual mockups produced for this spec. Auto-populated by "
"`/mock`\n"
"against the spec slug. Omit this section if no mockup was produced.\n"
"\n"
"- [Mockup name](.hero/mocks/{slug}/index.html) — YYYY-MM-DD — what the "
"mockup shows\n"
"\n"
"## Boundaries\n"
"What is NOT in scope. Adjacent work to explicitly avoid.\n"
"Things that look related but should be separate work items.\n"
"\n"
"## Risks\n"
"Known risks, edge cases, failure modes to watch for during "
"implementation.\n"
"Dependencies on external systems or teams.\n"
"\n"
"## Validation\n"
"How to verify the work is correct. Expected test coverage.\n"
"Manual verification steps if applicable.\n"
"Performance or operational checks if relevant.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:86
msgid "Bug spec template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:88
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"# {title}\n"
"\n"
"## Issue\n"
"Link to the bug ticket. Reporter. When it was found. Environment details."
"\n"
"\n"
"## Investigation\n"
"What was found during research. Evidence gathered.\n"
"Code traces — the end-to-end flow from trigger to failure.\n"
"Reproduction steps if applicable.\n"
"Key files and line numbers involved.\n"
"\n"
"### Root cause\n"
"Clear explanation of why the bug occurs. Distinguish between the symptom\n"
"and the underlying cause.\n"
"\n"
"### Severity\n"
"Impact, frequency, blast radius. Whether there is a workaround.\n"
"Whether this is caused by our code or an external factor.\n"
"\n"
"## Goal\n"
"What the fix accomplishes. One paragraph.\n"
"\n"
"## Changes\n"
"Ordered fix steps. Same format as feature changes — concrete, actionable,"
"\n"
"naming specific files and components.\n"
"\n"
"1. {description of first change}\n"
"   - {specific detail}\n"
"2. {description of second change}\n"
"   - {specific detail}\n"
"3. ...\n"
"\n"
"## Mockups\n"
"Optional. Visual mockups produced for this fix, if any. Auto-populated by"
"\n"
"`/mock` against the spec slug. Omit this section if no mockup was "
"produced.\n"
"\n"
"- [Mockup name](.hero/mocks/{slug}/index.html) — YYYY-MM-DD — what the "
"mockup shows\n"
"\n"
"## Boundaries\n"
"What this fix does NOT attempt to address.\n"
"Related issues that should be separate work items.\n"
"\n"
"## Risks\n"
"Regression risks. Side effects of the fix.\n"
"Areas that need careful testing.\n"
"\n"
"## Validation\n"
"How to verify the fix works. Regression test expectations.\n"
"How to confirm the original issue no longer reproduces.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:140
msgid "Mockups section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:142
msgid ""
"When `/mock` produces a visual prototype against a spec slug, it appends "
"(or updates, on `--iterate`) a `## Mockups` section in the spec body "
"listing each mockup. This makes the artifact discoverable to humans "
"reading the spec and to delivery agents reading the spec for context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:147
msgid ""
"**Format.** One entry per mockup, in a top-level `## Mockups` section "
"placed between `## Changes` and `## Boundaries`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:150
msgid ""
"## Mockups\n"
"\n"
"- [Hero landing page](.hero/mocks/hero-landing-page/index.html) — "
"2026-05-20 — public homepage with install CTA and feature grid\n"
"- [Hero landing page — dense variant](.hero/mocks/hero-landing-"
"page/dense.html) — 2026-05-22 — compressed-density alternative for above-"
"the-fold\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:157
msgid "**Rules:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:159
msgid "The section is optional — omit it entirely if no mockup was produced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:160
msgid "Path is relative to the repo root so the link works in markdown renderers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:161
msgid "Date is ISO format (`YYYY-MM-DD`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:162
msgid "Description is one line — what's shown, not why."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:163
msgid "Multiple mockups per spec are supported as additional list items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:164
msgid ""
"`/mock --iterate` updates the matching entry's date in place rather than "
"appending a duplicate when the path is unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:166
msgid ""
"Free-text `/mock` calls (no spec slug) do not write back — those mockups "
"land under `.hero/mocks/_adhoc/` and are not linked to any spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:169
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`/deliver` reads `.hero/mocks/{slug}/` directly as a pre-flight step, so "
"mockups generated before this section was introduced (or dropped in by "
"hand) are still surfaced to the engineer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:173
msgid "Convention spec template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:175
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"---\n"
"type: convention\n"
"status: active\n"
"scope: [glob patterns where this applies]\n"
"tags: [relevant tags]\n"
"---\n"
"# {Convention Name}\n"
"\n"
"## Pattern\n"
"What this convention standardizes. One clear statement.\n"
"\n"
"## When to apply\n"
"The conditions under which this convention must be followed.\n"
"File types, modules, or situations where it applies.\n"
"\n"
"## How\n"
"The specific implementation pattern to follow, with concrete examples\n"
"from this codebase.\n"
"\n"
"## Examples\n"
"Real examples from the codebase showing this pattern done correctly.\n"
"\n"
"## Anti-patterns\n"
"Common violations of this convention and why they're problematic.\n"
"\n"
"## Exceptions\n"
"When it's acceptable to deviate from this convention and why.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:205
msgid "Decision spec template (ADR)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:207
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"---\n"
"type: decision\n"
"status: accepted\n"
"tags: [relevant tags]\n"
"relates-to: [related-spec-slugs]\n"
"---\n"
"# {Decision Title}\n"
"\n"
"## Context\n"
"The situation and forces that led to this decision.\n"
"\n"
"## Options considered\n"
"Each option with pros, cons, and trade-offs.\n"
"\n"
"## Decision\n"
"What was chosen and why.\n"
"\n"
"## Consequences\n"
"What changes as a result. What becomes easier, what becomes harder.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:229
msgid "Initiative spec template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:231
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"---\n"
"type: initiative\n"
"status: planning\n"
"tags: [relevant tags]\n"
"---\n"
"# {Initiative Title}\n"
"\n"
"## Vision\n"
"What this initiative achieves when all parts are complete.\n"
"\n"
"## Specs\n"
"Ordered list of child specs, each a separate design/diagnose item.\n"
"Mark completion status.\n"
"\n"
"## Dependencies\n"
"Cross-spec dependencies and sequencing constraints.\n"
"\n"
"## Progress\n"
"Summary of what's done, what's in flight, what's next.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:253
msgid "Frontmatter conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:255
msgid "All spec types use YAML frontmatter. The following fields are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Required"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Applies to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`title`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "All"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Human-readable title."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`slug`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Short kebab-case identifier matching the spec's directory name. Stamp "
"this in frontmatter so it's easy to copy when linking the spec from "
"another session or prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`type`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Spec type: `feature`, `bug`, `convention`, `decision`, `initiative`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`status`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Lifecycle state. Work specs: `planning`, `in-review`, `delivering`, "
"`completed`. Conventions: `draft`, `active`. Decisions: `proposed`, "
"`accepted`. Any type can be `superseded`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`scope`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Yes (conventions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Convention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Array of glob patterns identifying which files this convention applies "
"to. Used by `hero relevant` to inject relevant conventions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`tags`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Array of tags for search and filtering. Use lowercase, hyphenated terms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`claimed_by`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Work specs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Who is currently working on this spec. Set via `hero spec claim`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`completed_at`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"RFC 3339 UTC timestamp recording when `status` flipped to `completed`. "
"Hero writes this automatically at status-transition time — agents and "
"humans should not hand-write it. The reader also accepts `completedAt:` "
"for tolerance, but only `completed_at:` is ever produced. Historical "
"specs without the field can be backfilled from git history via `hero "
"admin backfill-completed-at`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`created`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "ISO 8601 date when the spec was created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`relates-to`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Array of spec slugs that are related but not dependent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`depends-on`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Array of spec slugs that must be completed before this spec can proceed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`supersedes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Slug of the spec this one replaces. The superseded spec should have its "
"status set to `superseded`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`parent`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Slug of the initiative this spec belongs to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`child`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Initiatives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Array of spec slugs that are part of this initiative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`domain`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"DSKG namespace partition (`engineering`, `pm`, future packs). New specs "
"scaffolded by `/design` and `/diagnose` emit this from the active "
"workspace domain. Legacy specs without the field resolve to the workspace"
" default (`engineering` if no `domain:` is set in `hero.json`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`size`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Sized work specs (`feature`, `bug`, `enhancement`, `epic`, `initiative`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Declared effort tier on the shared 6-tier ladder: `trivial`, `small`, "
"`medium`, `large`, `x-large`, `giant`. Living field — set at design, "
"updated on scope changes (authoring and mid-delivery). See the `spec-"
"sizing` skill for the ladder, per-type bands, and the nudge protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`size_ack`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Sized work specs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"One-shot acknowledgement that suppresses the design-time nudge when a "
"spec stays at a high tier deliberately. Only `giant` is consumed today. "
"See the `spec-sizing` skill."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:277
msgid "`size:` — a living field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:279
msgid ""
"Treat `size:` like `status:` — agents are expected to keep it accurate. "
"Updates happen at design time (`/design` stamps it from the design "
"conversation), during authoring/refinement (the spec writer bumps it if "
"scope grows), and mid-delivery (the delivery lead bumps it if reality "
"outruns the declared tier)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:285
msgid "Brief frontmatter example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:287
msgid ""
"---\n"
"title: \"Add CSV export\"\n"
"type: feature\n"
"status: planning\n"
"size: medium\n"
"---\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:296
msgid ""
"Don't re-explain the ladder here — the canonical reference is the `spec-"
"sizing` skill. It carries the 6-tier descriptions, per-type bands, nudge "
"schedule, and the `size_ack: giant` acknowledgement protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:301
msgid "Status transitions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:303
msgid ""
"Work specs follow a linear progression: `planning` → `in-review` → "
"`delivering` → `completed`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:305
msgid ""
"Conventions start as `draft` while being authored and reviewed. They move"
" to `active` when the team confirms they reflect actual or intended "
"practice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:307
msgid ""
"Decisions start as `proposed` during discussion. They move to `accepted` "
"when the decision is finalized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:309
msgid ""
"Any spec can be set to `superseded` when a newer spec replaces it. Always"
" set the `supersedes` field on the replacement spec to maintain "
"traceability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:311
msgid "Acceptance Criteria and EARS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:313
msgid ""
"Acceptance criteria live in a `## Acceptance Criteria` section as a "
"bullet list. Hero recognizes five EARS (Easy Approach to Requirements "
"Syntax) patterns and classifies each bullet automatically; freeform "
"bullets remain valid for criteria that genuinely don't fit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Use when"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "**Event**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`WHEN <trigger> THE SYSTEM SHALL <behavior>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "A user action or external event produces a specific outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "**State**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`WHILE <state> THE SYSTEM SHALL <behavior>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "A condition holds for a span of time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "**Unwanted**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`IF <trigger> THEN THE SYSTEM SHALL <behavior>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "An error or guard condition must be handled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "**Optional**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`WHERE <feature> IS ENABLED THE SYSTEM SHALL <behavior>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "Behavior applies only under a feature flag or opt-in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "**Ubiquitous**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "`THE SYSTEM SHALL <behavior>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md
msgid "An always-true invariant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:326
msgid "Example (from a real feature spec):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:328
msgid ""
"## Acceptance Criteria\n"
"\n"
"- WHEN a user submits invalid form data THE SYSTEM SHALL display field-"
"level validation errors\n"
"- WHILE a sync is in flight THE SYSTEM SHALL block concurrent sync "
"attempts\n"
"- IF the tracker token is missing THEN THE SYSTEM SHALL print a setup "
"hint and exit non-zero\n"
"- WHERE auto_capture IS ENABLED THE SYSTEM SHALL persist learnings after "
"/deliver\n"
"- THE SYSTEM SHALL log every failed login attempt\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:338
msgid "**Guidelines:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:340
msgid "Keywords are case-insensitive, but uppercase reads best in review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:341
msgid "A trailing period is allowed but not required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:342
msgid ""
"Don't force EARS onto criteria where it reads awkwardly — freeform is "
"fine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:343
msgid "Run `hero spec lint <slug>` to see the classification + freeform ratio."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-format/SKILL.md:344
msgid ""
"`hero test generate` maps the `Behavior` clause to Playwright assertions,"
" so concrete identifiers (selectors, URLs, flag names) inside the "
"behavior produce better autonomous tests than vague phrasing."
